<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85619" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπ-εῖον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>vessel employed in solemn processions,</i> mostly pl.,
				<i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				22.48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπείων ἐπιστάται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12.379.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				124
			</span></i>; at Rome, <i>the apparatus of a triumph,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				43.42
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπεία σκευή</span> is dub.
			(leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπεῖα [σκεύη</span>]) in <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				12.40
			</span></i>: sg., of a wax <i>bust</i> of <i><span class="en">
				Cleopatra
			</span></i>
			<i>carried in triumph,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				51.21
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπείου τυχεῖν</span> to have
			one's <i>image carried in procession,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.38J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Athens, <i>storehouse
				where such vessels were kept,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				34.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.43
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				6.22
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
